66
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:22,880
Let's start off by asking the question, what is holography?

67
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:30,000
Holography is very similar to photography.

68
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:37,920
Except that when you look at a hologram, you see three dimensions.

69
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:46,000
With a photograph, you only have two dimensions.

70
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:55,400
For instance, if you had a photograph of an apple behind a box.

71
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:59,480
Par exemple, si vous avez une photograph d'une pomme derrière.

72
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:04,520
You would not be able to look around the box and see the apple behind it.

73
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,800
Because the photograph has height and width.

74
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:18,120
But does not have depth.

75
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:25,400
With a hologram, you would be able to move and look around the box.

76
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:32,120
And see the apple behind it.

77
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:40,440
Because the hologram contains height, width, and depth.

78
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:50,040
Let's examine what holography is used for.

79
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:28,520
Which stops other people from manufacturing cards.

80
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:36,280
You may actually have a hologram on a pair of jeans.

81
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:46,000
So you know that when you buy the jeans, they are made by who you think they are made from.

82
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:53,680
Don't jean, you saved the proper manufacturer, par exemple.

83
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:58,720
In medicine, holograms are used to show internal organs.

84
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:10,960
And doctors can actually go up inside and take measurements as if the organ were really there.

85
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:53,680
In commercial holography, you may find a hologram inside of a magazine.

86
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:02,560
Which shows a three-dimensional picture of the product.

87
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:14,560
In the future, you may have your favorite television show projected right into your living room.

88
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:29,160
Holograms are created using lasers.

89
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:36,200
It is only one of many uses of the laser.

90
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,280
Other uses include communications.

91
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:49,960
When you make a long distance telephone call, your voice travels over a laser beam.

92
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:01,640
Recently we've discovered new ways to make holograms.

